{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>לֹא אֲדֹנִי.</b> Meaning: you shall not take the cave alone, but the field as well I have already given — meaning, I have already resolved in my mind to give it. And his reason: the field would not be fit for anything once the cave serves as a burial site. And on this he was precise in saying ״שְׁמָעֵנִי״ — meaning, that he should understand his words and his reasoning." "<b>וְהַמְּעָרָה וְגוֹ׳.</b> Meaning: already in the first embassy, when the children of Heth answered him and said (Genesis 23:6) ״אִישׁ מִמֶּנּוּ אֶת קִבְרוֹ לֹא יִכְלֶה״ etc. — to you I have given it. And the reason he returned a second time to say <b>לְעֵינֵי</b> etc., is to say that no hesitation whatsoever remained from any legal claim regarding the cave that Abraham had been concerned about at the beginning of his words when he said (Genesis 23:8) ״וּפִגְעוּ לִי״ etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:42:53.261161681Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}